  {"h": "Wrangler JL steps with no Gladiator part number", "body": "Wikipedia lists the JT's wheelbase at 137.3 in against 118.4 in for the 4-door Wrangler, and Westin sells a separate part for each. Buy the part whose fit list names the Gladiator."},
  {"h": "Ordering before looking under the doors", "body": "Jeep's 2025 press kit lists steel rock rails on the Willys, Rubicon and Mojave. A rocker-mounted step may need them removed, as Rough Country's 90762 does."},
  {"h": "Drop steps on a trail truck", "body": "A 4 in drop plate under a 137.3 in wheelbase is the first thing to touch. Use a frame-mounted slider or a power step."},
